I replaced the per-call linear scan with a lazily built 65536-entry direct lookup table, preserving first-match semantics and NULL for unknown message numbers. After a one-time O(MESGS) fill, every lookup is O(1).

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const Profile::MESG* table[65536] = {};
    static bool initialized = false;

    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; ++i)
        {
            if (table[mesgs[i].num] == NULL)
            {
                table[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
            }
        }
        initialized = true;
    }

    return table[num];
}
```